### Disposable HTTPS fixture only; see README.acceptance.md.
### All values are placeholders; never use a real admin, existing database or profile.
### Choose {{fixtureTargetUserId}} from a user created in THIS fixture; never mutate
### the bootstrap admin or guess a numeric ID. Observe each request individually.

### List/filter users — 200 ADMIN, 403 USER
GET {{fixtureBaseUrl}}/api/admin/users?page=0&size=20&sortBy=createdAt&sortDir=desc
Authorization: Bearer {{fixtureAdminToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Create target — 201, generated one-time password, forced change, no-store
POST {{fixtureBaseUrl}}/api/admin/users
Authorization: Bearer {{fixtureAdminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "username": "{{fixtureNewUsername}}",
  "fullName": "Disposable admin-created user",
  "email": "{{fixtureNewEmail}}",
  "role": "USER"
}

### Detail — 200, no credentials
GET {{fixtureBaseUrl}}/api/admin/users/{{fixtureTargetUserId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{fixtureAdminToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Lock target — 200, previous target bearer now 401 on /me
PUT {{fixtureBaseUrl}}/api/admin/users/{{fixtureTargetUserId}}/lock
Authorization: Bearer {{fixtureAdminToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Unlock target — 200
PUT {{fixtureBaseUrl}}/api/admin/users/{{fixtureTargetUserId}}/unlock
Authorization: Bearer {{fixtureAdminToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Change target role — 200; immediately restore USER after observing
PUT {{fixtureBaseUrl}}/api/admin/users/{{fixtureTargetUserId}}/role
Authorization: Bearer {{fixtureAdminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "role": "ADMIN"
}

###
PUT {{fixtureBaseUrl}}/api/admin/users/{{fixtureTargetUserId}}/role
Authorization: Bearer {{fixtureAdminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "role": "USER"
}

### Reset — generated one-time password, forced-change. Do not save response.
PUT {{fixtureBaseUrl}}/api/admin/users/{{fixtureTargetUserId}}/reset-password
Authorization: Bearer {{fixtureAdminToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Read settings, snapshot original values for restoration
GET {{fixtureBaseUrl}}/api/admin/settings
Authorization: Bearer {{fixtureAdminToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Valid settings body; keep at least one link method enabled
PUT {{fixtureBaseUrl}}/api/admin/settings
Authorization: Bearer {{fixtureAdminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "settings": {
    "ALLOW_REGISTRATION": "false",
    "MAX_GMAIL_PER_USER": "5",
    "MAX_ATTACHMENT_SIZE_MB": "25"
  }
}

### Verify effective flags, perform valid register probe, restore saved values
GET {{fixtureBaseUrl}}/api/public/config
Accept: application/json

###
PUT {{fixtureBaseUrl}}/api/admin/settings
Authorization: Bearer {{fixtureAdminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "settings": {
    "ALLOW_REGISTRATION": "{{fixtureOriginalRegistrationFlag}}",
    "MAX_GMAIL_PER_USER": "{{fixtureOriginalGmailLimit}}",
    "MAX_ATTACHMENT_SIZE_MB": "{{fixtureOriginalAttachmentLimit}}"
  }
}

### Stats
GET {{fixtureBaseUrl}}/api/admin/stats
Authorization: Bearer {{fixtureAdminToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Audit filtered page; use synthetic target/actor only
GET {{fixtureBaseUrl}}/api/admin/logs?page=0&size=20&action=MAIL_DELETE
Authorization: Bearer {{fixtureAdminToken}}
Accept: application/json

### CSV export — correct media; do not save raw audit output
GET {{fixtureBaseUrl}}/api/admin/logs/export?action=MAIL_DELETE
Authorization: Bearer {{fixtureAdminToken}}
Accept: text/csv

### Negative Accept — expected 406 NOT_ACCEPTABLE in fixed source
GET {{fixtureBaseUrl}}/api/admin/logs/export?action=MAIL_DELETE
Authorization: Bearer {{fixtureAdminToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Delete only the explicitly created fixture target after all its checks — 204
DELETE {{fixtureBaseUrl}}/api/admin/users/{{fixtureTargetUserId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{fixtureAdminToken}}
Accept: application/json
